{# Announcement modal "xp_launch_reveal" (docs/features/announcement-modals.md, docs/features/xp-levels/launch-2026-10.md).
   Stays in the code for good - XpLaunchRevealRule decides who gets it and ResolveAnnouncementModal that nobody gets it
   twice. The modal is the reveal's first step, the level's chapter: the player puts the last piece into the level
   medallion and the XP counts up (XpLaunchRevealModal); members continue into their achievements, free players get the
   member tease (achievements are a membership feature - how many, never which).
   No "seen" report on opening (no seen-url): for this modal "seen" = the level was revealed, POSTed by the level's
   puzzle (xp_launch_level_revealed) - the reveal page leaves the level out of its deck then. #}
<div
    class="modal fade"
    tabindex="-1"
    role="dialog"
    id="announcement-modal"
    aria-labelledby="announcement-modal-title"
    data-controller="autoshow-modal"
    data-autoshow-modal-name-value="{{ announcement.value }}"
>
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered" role="document">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-body text-center px-3 px-sm-4 pt-2 pb-4">
                <twig:XpLaunchRevealModal
                    playerId="{{ logged_user.profile.playerId }}"
                    :isMember="logged_user.profile.activeMembership"
                />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
